WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.145 --> 00:00:03.130
- So I saw the new Star
Wars film this weekend,

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.072
(buzzer)

00:00:04.072 --> 00:00:06.393
and I've got some issues.

00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:09.143
(dramatic music)

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.821
Seriously, if you haven't
seen the movie yet,

00:00:15.821 --> 00:00:17.988
I'm gonna spoil all of it.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.090
(whirring)

00:00:22.952 --> 00:00:24.217
I'm a Star Wars fan.

00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:26.865
But I think it's far
from a perfect series.

00:00:26.865 --> 00:00:28.860
- Mesa called Jar-Jar Binks.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.933
- And there were a lot of things
about The Last Jedi I liked

00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:35.026
like Kylo and Rey taking on Snoke,

00:00:35.026 --> 00:00:36.412
puppet Yoda.

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:39.633
But at the same time,
there were a lot of things

00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:42.035
I did not care for.

00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:44.368
First, the entire Finn plot.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:46.728
- Where's Rey?

00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:49.822
- A lot of the film is
dedicated to this plot line,

00:00:49.822 --> 00:00:51.449
and it never works out.

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:52.781
The plan fails,

00:00:52.781 --> 00:00:56.652
and its failure has no effect
on the rest of the story.

00:00:56.652 --> 00:00:59.179
And seriously, the whole plot
line would've been solved

00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:02.314
if Finn and Rose just took a few minutes

00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:04.515
to find a parking spot.

00:01:04.515 --> 00:01:07.682
Next, Leia Supermanning through space.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.256
Third, and this is a big one for me,

00:01:14.256 --> 00:01:17.840
when did Jedi suddenly
have unlimited power?

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.655
Rey and Kylo spend most of this film

00:01:20.655 --> 00:01:23.343
Force FaceTiming with each other.

00:01:23.343 --> 00:01:26.559
And Luke suddenly has the
ability to project his spirit

00:01:26.559 --> 00:01:29.206
worlds away from his actual location.

00:01:29.206 --> 00:01:31.609
When did these become things?

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:34.776
Fourth, Laura Dern's entire existence.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.390
Why is she in this movie?

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.734
And why does her character look like

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:41.712
she fell out of The
Hunger Games Franchise?

00:01:41.712 --> 00:01:44.404
Admirable Ackbar should've
been the one that took

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.075
control of The Resistance,

00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:47.458
and he should've been the one

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:49.494
that went on the suicide mission.

00:01:49.494 --> 00:01:51.895
Because that way, we would've cared.

00:01:51.895 --> 00:01:54.478
Next, Porgs and Crystal Wolves?

00:01:56.698 --> 00:01:57.531
Shut up.

00:01:58.575 --> 00:02:01.242
And lastly, the end of the film.

00:02:02.525 --> 00:02:05.584
Luke just disappears, really?

00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:06.972
Like, I get it,

00:02:06.972 --> 00:02:09.459
Luke can't live up to his own legend,

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:11.987
and there's also an argument
for religious allegory,

00:02:11.987 --> 00:02:13.048
blah, blah, blah.

00:02:13.048 --> 00:02:17.693
Luke is one of the greatest
heroes in cinematic history,

00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:20.995
and the guy just fades away into a sunset

00:02:20.995 --> 00:02:22.700
because he's exhausted?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.596
(record scratch)

00:02:23.596 --> 00:02:26.775
Oh, and Luke milking that cow thing,

00:02:26.775 --> 00:02:28.608
what was that?

00:02:28.608 --> 00:02:31.275
(playful music)

